/* MvMediaPicker — "Adicionar foto ou vídeo": dashed empty state -> thumbnail grid.
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §6 row 5, §8.5 "Adicionar foto ou vídeo".
 * Figma: `Dashed Upload Box` 109:970 (Tela 11) — 358x112, V, gap 8, pad 20,
 * centered, surface fill, r16, 1px outline-variant dashed [6,6];
 * `Populated Upload Box` 109:1117 (Tela 12) — 358x274, V, gap 12, pad 16, r16,
 * 1px outline-variant; `Image Grid` 109:4184 — H, wrap, gap 8;
 * `User Upload n` — 104x104 r12 with `Delete Button` 28x28 r14 at top/right 4,
 * scrim @ 25%, 14dp close glyph; `Add More` 109:4197 — 104x104 r12, surface-dim
 * fill, 1px outline-variant dashed [4,4], 24dp add_circle.
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * THE DASHED BORDERS ARE PAINTED, NOT DECLARED
 *   USS exposes border width, color and radius — there is no `border-style`, so a
 *   dashed edge is impossible to declare. MvDashedOutline (in the .cs) paints one
 *   with Painter2D from its own resolved `color` and `border-radius`, which is why
 *   `.mv-media-picker__dash` below carries a color and a radius but no width: the
 *   width is the painter's, the rest stays the designer's. The struct dumps under
 *   .figma-sync/struct/ do NOT record strokeDashes — both dashed edges are only
 *   visible in file.json and in the PNG renders. Do not "correct" them to solid.
 *
 * WIDTH IS THE CALLER'S — V2's 358 is the form column, not a property of the
 * picker (same rule as MvAlertBar / MvOptionCard). Heights are ours.
 *
 * THREE TILES DO NOT FIT ON A ROW, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN'S ARITHMETIC
 *   The grid's content width is 326 (358 form column - 2x16 card padding) and V2
 *   asks for 104dp tiles with 8dp gaps: 3*104 + 2*8 = 328 > 326. Figma only fits
 *   three by silently shrinking the first tile to 102 (see `User Upload 1`'s
 *   absoluteBoundingBox). Flexbox has no such move — `flex-wrap` breaks a line
 *   before it shrinks anything — so the literal 104dp tile from §8.5 is kept and
 *   the third tile wraps. Two ways out when multi-photo actually ships (Decision
 *   D6; the cap is 1 for now, so at most one tile ever renders here): drop the
 *   gap to 7dp, which makes 3*104 + 2*7 = 326 exactly, or make the tile size a
 *   property and compute it from the measured width. Neither is worth doing blind.
 *
 * NEGATIVE MARGINS ARE THE ROW/COLUMN GUTTER
 *   USS has no `gap`, and the margin-on-every-item-except-the-first trick
 *   (MvNumberedList, MvHeroHeader's badges) breaks under `flex-wrap`: "first" is
 *   the first of the whole grid, so every later ROW would start with an indent.
 *   Uniform trailing margins plus a matching negative margin on the grid is the
 *   only variant that survives wrapping.
 *
 * INK COLOR
 *   V2 paints the call-to-action line in the brand navy, the same ink as every
 *   form section label — the swatch Appendix A.1 maps to `primary`. As ink on a
 *   white card that collapses onto `on-surface`, the same collapse A.1 makes for
 *   the mid-grey body color, and what MdCard/MdChip already use. `primary` itself
 *   would be an M3 role violation for body text and would turn the label pale
 *   blue in the dark theme.
 *
 * THE REMOVE BUTTON IS 28dp, NOT A 48dp TOUCH TARGET
 *   Deliberate, and the one place this library breaks its own minimum. The button
 *   lives INSIDE a 104dp tile with `overflow: hidden`, so a larger root would
 *   either cover a quarter of the photo it annotates or be clipped back to 28dp
 *   for picking as well as for painting. V2 draws 28.
 */

.mv-media-picker {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
}

/* ---- Empty state ---- */

.mv-media-picker__empty {
    min-height: 112px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-large);
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface);
    /* Required by the state-layer contract, and it also trims the outer half of
     * the painted dash stroke — MvDashedOutline insets by half a line width. */
    overflow: hidden;
}

.mv-media-picker__empty:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
}

/* Both dashed edges. Radius is read back by the painter, so it must be declared
 * here even though nothing draws a real border. */
.mv-media-picker__dash {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-large);
}

.mv-media-picker__empty-icon {
    font-size: 24px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* label-large metrics (14px / ls 0) at V2's 600 face. §8.5 says 700; all four
 * Reportar frames (Tela 3, 5, 11, 12) draw this string at Inter 600 — the frames win. */
.mv-media-picker__empty-title {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-SemiBold.asset");
}

/* body-small metrics (12px / ls 0). Shown in BOTH states — 12dp under the grid,
 * 8dp under the call to action — and aligned DIFFERENTLY in each: V2 flushes it
 * to the grid's left edge on the filled card (the base rule here) and centres it
 * under the call to action in the dashed box (the override below). */
.mv-media-picker__hint {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-align: middle-left;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-Regular.asset");
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
}

.mv-media-picker__empty .mv-media-picker__hint {
    margin-top: 8px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* ---- Filled state ---- */

.mv-media-picker__card {
    padding: 16px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-large);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface);
}

.mv-media-picker__grid {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    /* Reclaims the trailing gutter the tiles' uniform margins add. */
    margin-right: -8px;
    margin-bottom: -8px;
}

.mv-media-picker__tile {
    width: 104px;
    height: 104px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-right: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-medium);
    overflow: hidden;
}

.mv-media-picker__thumb {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
}

.mv-media-picker__remove {
    position: absolute;
    top: 4px;
    right: 4px;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-full);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.mv-media-picker__remove:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
}

/* V2's pure black at 25% (§8 "remove 28x28, pure black at 0.25, r14"). `scrim` is the
 * only pure-black role and is identical in both themes; the alpha is an `opacity` on
 * this layer alone, so the glyph above it stays opaque (a literal translucent color
 * would fail TokenDisciplineTests anyway).
 *
 * 0.47 AUTHORED, NOT 0.25 — LINEAR-SPACE CORRECTION, AND IT GOES UP NOT DOWN.
 * The 0.25 is a Figma alpha and Figma blends in sRGB; Unity renders in LINEAR color
 * space (ProjectSettings m_ActiveColorSpace: 1), so the same alpha composites LIGHTER
 * — the disc was rendering up to 28/255 per channel too pale, which is precisely the
 * contrast the white glyph needs to survive a bright photo. Counter-intuitively a DARK
 * overlay needs its alpha RAISED (a light one needs it cut ~3.5x); the correction is
 * not a uniform "reduce".
 *
 * WHY THIS STAYS AN ALPHA WHILE THE camera-* TOKENS DID NOT: those sit on opaque,
 * known surfaces, so the exact composite can be authored as a color. This one sits on
 * an arbitrary USER PHOTO, so there is nothing to pre-blend against and a real alpha
 * is the only correct form. 0.47 is the per-channel corrected alpha averaged over a
 * 7-photo tone sweep; it reproduces the Figma composite to within 2/255 everywhere on
 * that sweep (the old 0.25 was off by up to 28). 0.25 is the INPUT, not a value to
 * restore. */
.mv-media-picker__remove-fill {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-scrim);
    opacity: 0.47;
}

/* `primary-fixed` is the near-white end of M3's *-fixed family, whose defining
 * property is that it does NOT flip between light and dark — exactly what a glyph
 * painted over user photos and a black scrim needs. `on-primary` would be the
 * literal white V2 draws in light theme but turns dark navy in the dark one, and
 * would vanish against the scrim. */
.mv-media-picker__remove-icon {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--md-sys-color-primary-fixed);
}

.mv-media-picker__add {
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface-dim);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
}

.mv-media-picker__add:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
}

.mv-media-picker__add .mv-media-picker__dash {
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-medium);
}

.mv-media-picker__add-icon {
    font-size: 24px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* ---- Interaction states ----
 * Three independent tap targets: the empty box, the add tile, each remove button. */

.mv-media-picker__empty .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__add .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
}

.mv-media-picker__remove .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary-fixed);
}

.mv-media-picker__empty:hover .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__add:hover .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__remove:hover .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-hover-opacity);
}
.mv-media-picker__empty:focus .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__add:focus .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__remove:focus .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-focus-opacity);
}
.mv-media-picker__empty:active .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__add:active .md-state-layer,
.mv-media-picker__remove:active .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-pressed-opacity);
}

/* ---- Disabled ---- */

.mv-media-picker__empty:disabled {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-content);
}
.mv-media-picker__empty:disabled .mv-media-picker__dash,
.mv-media-picker__add:disabled .mv-media-picker__dash {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-container);
}
.mv-media-picker__add:disabled {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-content);
}
